            <ArticleTitle>[Primary epiploic appendicitis: an etiology of acute abdomen revealed by CT scan].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>333-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Primary epiploic appendicitis are considered to be a rare cause of acute abdomen. We reported 2 cases in which computed tomography CT suggested the diagnosis. Primary epiploic appendicitis shows characteristic CT findings that allow the diagnosis and follow-up. This entity resolves spontaneously and CT helps in avoiding unnecessary surgery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
